@startuml
!theme plain
left to right direction
hide empty description
title User-visible VPN Connection State Contract

state "Disconnected" as Disconnected
state "Connecting" as Connecting
state "Connected / Full" as Full
state "Connected / Degraded" as Degraded
state "Reasserting" as Reasserting
state "Disconnecting" as Disconnecting
state "Failed" as Failed

[*] --> Disconnected

Disconnected --> Connecting : explicit connect\neligible profile + disclosure
Connecting --> Full : session connected\ncurrent generation has TCP + safe DNS + UDP
Connecting --> Degraded : session connected\ncurrent generation has TCP + safe DNS, no UDP
Connecting --> Failed : mandatory startup failure
Connecting --> Disconnecting : explicit stop

Full --> Degraded : relay/UDP lost\nbase TCP + safe DNS remain
Degraded --> Full : validated relay generation restored

Full --> Reasserting : path/transport/settings recovery
Degraded --> Reasserting : mandatory base recovery begins
Reasserting --> Full : current generation fully restored
Reasserting --> Degraded : current generation safely degraded
Reasserting --> Failed : bounded recovery ends unsafely

Full --> Disconnecting : explicit stop
Degraded --> Disconnecting : explicit stop
Reasserting --> Disconnecting : explicit stop
Failed --> Connecting : explicit retry
Failed --> Disconnected : acknowledge / clear failed attempt
Disconnecting --> Disconnected : system confirms stop

note top of Full
  Full requires a fresh provider capability snapshot.
  Cached app state cannot create this state.
end note

note bottom of Degraded
  Still connected: eligible TCP and leak-safe DNS continue.
  General UDP is unavailable and must be named explicitly.
end note

note bottom of Failed
  Reserved for a requirement without which
  safe forwarding cannot continue.
end note

@enduml